# From "Meeting with the Entry Director" (Wave VIII - Union, CD1-2): the
# personal, historical counterpart to planning-center.gws's collective focus
# -- your own entry into this lifetime, not the planning center's role for
# Earth as a whole.

@segment  meeting-with-the-entry-director
@title    Meeting with the Entry Director
@levels   F27
@duration ~4m30s

say Move to the Planning Center now. Ask to meet with the entry director, and others who help prepare people for entry into physical earth life.
pause 8
say Make contact. Use every sense you have.
pause 8
say Ask to observe the process itself -- the steps in preparing to enter a physical body, a new human life. Notice anything that surprises you. Listen. Absorb.
pause 10
say Now ask to meet anyone here with direct knowledge of your own personal history -- anyone who knows you well.
pause 8
say With that contact made, ask for a review of your own entry into this life. What discussions took place? What choices did you make in preparing for it? What were you meant to learn from this lifetime? What guidance were you given? What were you feeling? What were your attitudes about it?
pause 15
say Let yourself fully experience this -- your entry into this life, and into others, if that's offered too.
hold 60
